  shortStory: "A Cyclops, in Greek mythology and later Roman mythology, was a member
    of a primordial race of giants, each with a single eye in the center of his forehead.
    The word \u201Ccyclops\u201D literally means \u201Cround-eyed or \u201Ccircle-eyed\u201D.\r\n\r\nIn
    a famous episode of Homer\u2019s Odyssey, the hero Odysseus encounters the cyclops
    Polyphemus, the son of Poseidon and Thoosa, who lives with his fellow cyclopes
    in a distant country.\r"
